---
description: Catalog rules use X/Y in parentheses; concrete values belong on units
alwaysApply: true
---

# Parameterized rule names

General catalog entries (`SpecialAbility`, `Rule`, `SpecialRule`) that take a numeric, dice, or distance value in parentheses must use **X** (and **Y** for a second value). Never put a concrete value on the catalog row or in its description.

```
✅ Elite (X)          ❌ Elite (2)
✅ Synapse (X)        ❌ Synapse (15 cm)
✅ Confusion (-X)     ❌ Confusion (-2)
✅ Dodge (X+)         ❌ Dodge (5+)
✅ Damage (+X) in Assault
✅ Damages Buildings (AP -X / Y)
```

Named variants that are different rules keep their words: `Slave (Hunt)`, `Forward Observer (FO)`.

Units and weapons store the concrete value in `AbilityValue` on the junction table. The profile shows `Elite (+2)` or `Synapse (15 cm)`; tapping it opens the catalog `Elite (X)` / `Synapse (X)` rule.

`RuleLinkifier` must treat `Name (X)` and `Name (+2)` as the same rule.
